# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Yuji Ikeda et al. (2026). Machine-Learning Interatomic Potentials Achieving CCSD(T) Accuracy for Systems with Extended Covalent Networks and van der Waals Interactions.
#   Journal of Chemical Theory and Computation. doi:10.1021/acs.jctc.5c02045  arXiv:2508.14306v3
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2508.14306v3 (sha256 aa9eef4dbacbd757...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 340 (Method/model). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/ikeda2026achieving.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the PNO-LCCSD(T)-F12 reference on hydrogen-terminated
# COF fragments and their vdW multimers (Table I), the four Delta-MTP
# training sets #2-#5 (up to 2-5 benzene rings) at MTP levels 8, 12, 16
# and 20 (cutoff 7 A), and the per-atom energy RMSEs of Table II on the
# training, validation and test sets. The MTP is fitted to the difference
# between PNO-LCCSD(T)-F12 and GFN2-xTB energies; the errors are those of
# TB+Delta-MTP against the CCSD(T)-level reference. Atomization energies,
# bond lengths, vibrational frequencies and COF properties are properties.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

###############################################################################
# Q1 -- Bibliographic identification
###############################################################################

entity:study-ikeda2026achieving a mlips:BenchmarkStudy ;
    rdfs:label "Ikeda et al. (2026): Delta-learned MTPs on a GFN2-xTB baseline reaching PNO-LCCSD(T)-F12 accuracy for an extended covalent organic framework" ;
    mlips:reportedIn entity:article-ikeda2026achieving .

